{"case_id":"C055","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["API protocol","input semantics"],"commit_induced":"YES","maintenance_needed":true,"confidence":99,"affected_functions":["LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput","fpixCopy","dpixCopy","fpixLinearCombination","dpixLinearCombination"],"reason":"S1 changes fpixCopy and dpixCopy from two-argument APIs to one-argument APIs, while H0 still calls both with two arguments, so S1 + H0 cannot build and reach the fuzzed behavior. S1 also removes the distinct-destination mode used by H0 for both linear-combination functions. These incompatibilities did not exist under S0 and were directly introduced by the commit.","evidence":["H0 calls dpixCopy(NULL, dpix_payload) repeatedly and fpixCopy(NULL, fpix_payload) repeatedly, but S1 declares dpixCopy(DPIX *dpixs) and fpixCopy(FPIX *fpixs).","H0 calls dpixLinearCombination(dpix_copy6, dpix1, dpix2, 1.1, 1.2), where dpix_copy6 is distinct from dpix1; S1 rejects dpixd && dpixd != dpixs1 as \"invalid inplace operation\".","H0 calls fpixLinearCombination(fpix_copy3, fpix5, fpix6, 1.1, 1.1), where fpix_copy3 is distinct from fpix5; S1 likewise rejects this mode.","S0 explicitly supported null or distinct destinations in fpixCopy, dpixCopy, fpixLinearCombination, and dpixLinearCombination; S1 removes those modes."],"recommended_action":"Update H0 to call fpixCopy(fpixs) and dpixCopy(dpixs), and invoke fpixLinearCombination and dpixLinearCombination with either a null destination or a destination identical to the first source; retain and destroy the returned objects correctly."}
